      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A model estimates that the initial number of photons in an $X$-ray beam is 600 when the beam\nreaches the surface of a certain material. The model also estimates that when the beam passes\nthrough this material, the number of photons in the beam decreases by $50\\%$ for each 13\nmillimeters of the material the beam passes through. Which equation represents this model, where\n$I$ is the estimated number of photons in the beam when the beam reaches a point $x$ millimeters\nfrom the surface?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-7a526cc861424c46ac55d6032fe95322",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q6"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$I=600(0.5)x/13$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$I=600(0.5)x$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$I=600(2)x/13$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$I=600(13)x/2$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
